From 4ddbdec0a07a1f437ee3318799b1417f975ec799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gtex-port <igomezv0921@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:45:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: sc2723-fgu: SC2723 PMIC fuel gauge (v48)

The SM-T280's battery state: voltage and current from the PMIC's fuel gauge,
calibrated with the A-die efuse's 4.2 V reading (one point, as the vendor's
sci_efuse_fgu_cal_get()); capacity from the coulomb counter, starting at the
percentage the vendor kernel keeps in the FGU's battery-backed user area (or
the power-on OCV through the battery's OCV table), written back every minute.
Battery data (3950 mAh, OCV table, 250 mOhm) from the vendor DTS.

Checked against the vendor kernel under TWRP: 2810 counts = 4049 mV (vendor
4048), 0x24A2 = 427 mA (vendor 429).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
